    <bpmn:process id="W_W4844" name="W4844. License/Permit Governance, Ownership Matrix &amp; Accountability" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Strategy (W4841); org change; lapse incident (accountability review)
Frequency: Annual + on change
Volume: 1 ownership matrix; ~all authorizations assigned
Owner: VP Legal &amp; Compliance / Chief Compliance Officer
Participants: Domain compliance owners, Store Ops (VS-07), DC Ops (VS-04), HR, Tax, HSE
Source: workflow W4844 — License/Permit Governance, Ownership Matrix &amp; Accountability</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4844_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4844_Lane1" name="Compliance Portfolio Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4844_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4844_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4844_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4844_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4844_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4844_Start3" name="Strategy (W4841); org change; lapse incident (accountability review)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4844_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4844_Task4" name="Maintain the ownership/RACI matrix: for every authorization class, the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Maintain the ownership/RACI matrix: for every authorization class, the Accountable executive (single throat-to-choke), the Responsible owner (domain team / site), Consulted (Legal/Finance), and Informed; assign each of the thousands of authorizations to an owner in the register (W4842)
Responsible (R): Compliance Portfolio Manager / Legal
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Annual + continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4844_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4844_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4844_Task5" name="Enforce accountability via the renewal workflow (W4845/W4849): owner is…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Enforce accountability via the renewal workflow (W4845/W4849): owner is notified on the tiered alerts, owns the renewal filing, and is accountable for lapse; escalate un-owned or orphaned authorizations; integrate with performance objectives
Responsible (R): Compliance Portfolio Manager / Domain Owners
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4844_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4844_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4844_Task6" name="Review accountability after any lapse/penalty incident (W4853/W4858)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Review accountability after any lapse/penalty incident (W4853/W4858): root-cause the ownership failure, adjust the matrix, and reinforce; report accountability-health to governance (W4864)
Responsible (R): Compliance Portfolio Manager / Internal Audit (VS-21)
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Per incident + annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4844_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4844_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4844_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4844_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-169 (ensure enterprise license/permit register integrity.) | - CTL-728: every authorization has a single Accountable owner; renewals owner-routed; lapse incidents root-caused
Owner: VP Legal &amp; Compliance / Chief Compliance Officer</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
