    <bpmn:process id="W_W4847" name="W4847. Regulatory Change Monitoring &amp; Impact-to-Portfolio Assessment" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Regulatory change (new law/IRR/circular); regulator bulletin; annual review
Frequency: Continuous + on change
Volume: ~60–100 regulatory changes tracked per year across all regulators (BIR/DOLE/DENR/DTI/LGU)
Owner: Regulatory Intelligence Analyst / Government Affairs (VS-104)
Participants: Domain compliance owners, Legal (VS-100.3), Strategy (VS-33)
Source: workflow W4847 — Regulatory Change Monitoring &amp; Impact-to-Portfolio Assessment</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4847_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4847_Lane1" name="Regulatory Intelligence">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4847_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4847_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4847_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4847_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4847_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4847_Start3" name="Regulatory change (new law/IRR/circular); regulator bulletin; annual review">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4847_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4847_Task4" name="Monitor regulatory change across all relevant regulators (BIR, DTI/BPS, DENR…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monitor regulatory change across all relevant regulators (BIR, DTI/BPS, DENR, DOLE, BFP, LGU, BSP, FDA/FPA/BPI, NPC, PCAB/CIAP, PEZA/BOI, LTO/LTFRB, BOI/PEZA, energy) via Government Affairs (VS-104), subscriptions, and associations; log each change
Responsible (R): Regulatory Intelligence / Government Affairs
Accountable (A): Compliance Portfolio Manager
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4847_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4847_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4847_Task5" name="Assess impact to the portfolio: which authorizations/sites/activities are…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Assess impact to the portfolio: which authorizations/sites/activities are affected, the required action (new permit, renewal-rule change, condition change, fee change, decommission), the deadline, and the owner (W4844); prioritize by impact and feed to the obligation map (W4843) and register (W4842)
Responsible (R): Regulatory Intelligence / Domain Owners / Legal
Accountable (A): Compliance Portfolio Manager
Duration: Per change</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4847_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4847_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4847_Task6" name="Track change-adoption to closure: confirm the required action is executed by…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Track change-adoption to closure: confirm the required action is executed by the owner (W4849/W4851/W4856), update the register/obligation map, and report change-adoption to governance (W4864); capture emerging regulatory risk for ERM (VS-21.2)
Responsible (R): Regulatory Intelligence / Domain Owners / Risk
Accountable (A): Compliance Portfolio Manager
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4847_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4847_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4847_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4847_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-169 (ensure enterprise license/permit register integrity.) | - CTL-728: regulatory changes logged &amp; impact-assessed; adoption tracked to closure; emerging risk fed to ERM
Owner: Regulatory Intelligence Analyst / Government Affairs (VS-104)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
