    <bpmn:process id="W_W4848" name="W4848. Portfolio Risk Tiering, Single-Points-of-Failure &amp; Resilience" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual ERM cycle (VS-21.2); lapse incident (W4853); concentration review
Frequency: Annual + on incident
Volume: 1 portfolio risk view; ~all authorizations tiered
Owner: Compliance Portfolio Manager / Risk (VS-21.2)
Participants: Domain owners, Legal (VS-100.3), BCP (VS-26), Internal Audit (VS-21)
Source: workflow W4848 — Portfolio Risk Tiering, Single-Points-of-Failure &amp; Resilience</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4848_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4848_Lane1" name="Compliance Portfolio Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4848_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4848_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4848_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4848_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4848_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4848_Start3" name="Annual ERM cycle (VS-21.2); lapse incident (W4853); concentration review">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4848_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4848_Task4" name="Tier the portfolio by risk: business impact (store-closing, bid-blocking…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Tier the portfolio by risk: business impact (store-closing, bid-blocking, service-blocking, fleet-blocking, fines), regulator scrutiny, and historical lapse/penalty rate; identify high-risk authorizations for heightened oversight (more frequent review, backup owner)
Responsible (R): Compliance Portfolio Manager / Risk / Domain Owners
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4848_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4848_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4848_Task5" name="Identify single-points-of-failure: a sole owner, a sole regulator-relationship…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Identify single-points-of-failure: a sole owner, a sole regulator-relationship, a sole third-party permit-service provider (W4854), a site with a sole critical permit, or a personnel credential with no backup (links to VS-165 W4835); build redundancy/continuity for each
Responsible (R): Compliance Portfolio Manager / Risk / BCP
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4848_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4848_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4848_Task6" name="Build portfolio resilience: BCP for regulator-outage/portal-down (VS-26)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Build portfolio resilience: BCP for regulator-outage/portal-down (VS-26), continuity workarounds for lapsed permits (W4853), alternative permit-service providers (W4854), and cross-training of owners; feed resilience gaps to ERM (VS-21.2) and BCP (VS-26)
Responsible (R): Compliance Portfolio Manager / BCP / Domain Owners
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Annual + continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4848_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4848_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4848_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4848_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-728 (ensure controlled execution — Portfolio Strategy, Inventory, Governance &amp; Regulatory Intelligence (PA-166.1).) | - CTL-728: portfolio risk-tiered; single-points-of-failure addressed; resilience linked to BCP (VS-26)
Owner: Compliance Portfolio Manager / Risk (VS-21.2)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W4848_Assoc9" sourceRef="W4848_Annotation8" targetRef="W4848_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
